  "requirement": "The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST tell agents that the requirements commit may fail validation until evidence is authored, and that only the pull request as a whole must pass.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation: the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST tell agents that (a) the requirements commit may fail validation until evidence is authored, and (b) only the pull request as a whole must pass.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_expects_the_requirements_commit_to_fail_validation]` carries the `{test}` reference. It calls `assert_phrases(\"habeas-requirements\", ...)`. That helper reads `bundled_skill(name)`, which is the skill's `SKILL.md` plus its reference files with whitespace collapsed. It then runs `assert_text`, which does `assert!(text.contains(phrase))`. The phrase it requires is \"This commit fails validation until evidence is authored; that is expected, as only the pull request as a whole must pass\".\n\nThis single phrase covers both clauses. It says the commit fails validation until evidence is authored, and that only the pull request as a whole must pass. The assertion is a real `contains` check on the skill the requirement names, so the test would fail if the guidance were removed or reworded.\n\nThe requirement has no other conditions, modes or boundary cases. The test skill is the right one, and the assertion is correct. I found no gap and no marking gap.",
